From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: quote _linked_into in _WEBKIT_TARGET_LINK_FRAMEWORK

When a framework is linked into nothing, ${_linked_into} is empty and the
condition expands to "WTF STREQUAL" and "NOT IN_LIST <list>". CMake 4.4
rejects that ("if given arguments ... Unknown arguments specified") and
configuring JavaScriptCore stops. Quoting keeps each operand present.

--- a/Source/cmake/WebKitMacros.cmake	2026-11-13 13:14:30.072852556 +0100
+++ b/Source/cmake/WebKitMacros.cmake	2026-11-13 13:14:30.080134473 +0100
@@ -308,7 +308,7 @@
         get_property(_linked_into GLOBAL PROPERTY ${framework}_LINKED_INTO)
 
         # See if the target is linking a framework that the specified framework is already linked into
-        if ((NOT _linked_into) OR (${framework} STREQUAL ${_linked_into}) OR (NOT ${_linked_into} IN_LIST ${_target}_FRAMEWORKS))
+        if ((NOT _linked_into) OR ("${framework}" STREQUAL "${_linked_into}") OR (NOT "${_linked_into}" IN_LIST ${_target}_FRAMEWORKS))
             list(APPEND ${_target}_PRIVATE_LIBRARIES WebKit::${framework})
 
             # The WebKit:: alias targets do not propagate OBJECT libraries so the
